WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:14.220
- [Mark] All right, Madison.

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:15.240
Madison, where'd you grow up?

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:16.699
Where are you from originally?

00:00:16.699 --> 00:00:17.830
From Tampa, Florida.

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:19.497
- [Mark] Tampa, and tell
me about your family.

00:00:19.497 --> 00:00:21.593
You had both of your
parents when you were a kid?

00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:28.420
- My mom and my mom's
boyfriend at the time,

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:30.170
but then she got married.

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:31.003
So it was my stepdad,

00:00:31.003 --> 00:00:34.450
but my dad, we were gone
'cause he went to prison

00:00:35.491 --> 00:00:36.937
when I was a kid.

00:00:36.937 --> 00:00:39.390
- [Mark] What did your
dad go to prison for?

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:41.799
- Domestic violence, yeah.

00:00:41.799 --> 00:00:44.383
He was an alcoholic, drank a lot.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:46.773
- [Mark] How was your childhood?

00:00:47.990 --> 00:00:52.210
- I got moved out of my
parents' house when I was 13,

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:55.320
'cause my stepdad used
to, you know, molest me.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:01:00.010
And so my mom chose me to
leave and my stepdad stayed.

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:02.423
So they put me in foster
care when I was 13.

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:04.390
- [Mark] And how are things after you went

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:05.800
to the foster system?

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:07.050
- I would run away a lot.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.180
Ran away to the streets and stuff

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:14.430
'cause I didn't wanna,
I didn't wanna be...

00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:15.590
If I couldn't be with my parents

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:18.140
I didn't wanna be anywhere.

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:19.008
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:01:19.008 --> 00:01:19.950
- You know.

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:22.210
- [Mark] And when you ran
away from the foster system,

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:23.720
where would you go?

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:26.697
- I'd go like with pimps or with...

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:32.040
cause pimps, they, you know, they were...

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:33.340
They knew how to maneuver me.

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:34.720
I was under age.

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:37.980
And so they knew how to like keep me

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:40.710
away from the police, and
that's where I, you know,

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:43.163
wanted to be, was low profile.

00:01:44.444 --> 00:01:46.283
- [Mark] So sex work
started early for you.

00:01:47.230 --> 00:01:48.350
And how about drugs?

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:50.150
Were drugs part of the
picture back then, too?

00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:53.523
- Yeah. Cocaine, crack.

00:01:58.870 --> 00:02:00.624
Not heroin just yet.

00:02:00.624 --> 00:02:01.874
Until I was 19.

00:02:03.695 --> 00:02:06.030
- [Mark] And who introduced
you to those drugs?

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:07.621
- The men, the pimps and stuff.

00:02:07.621 --> 00:02:08.454
- [Mark] The pimps?

00:02:08.454 --> 00:02:09.970
- Yeah.

00:02:09.970 --> 00:02:11.730
- [Mark] This was in Tampa?

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:14.073
- Tampa, Georgia.

00:02:15.818 --> 00:02:19.203
And I mean, yeah, we would
travel all on the East Coast.

00:02:22.665 --> 00:02:25.120
- [Mark] And you came
out to LA at which point?

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:28.483
- When I got out of prison when I was 23.

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:35.390
So 20 years, 24 when I was 20, almost 24

00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:36.660
I moved out to California.

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:38.720
- [Mark] What were you doing in prison?

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:40.053
- Residue on a spoon.

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:46.320
I got caught with residue
of heroin on a spoon.

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:48.890
They gave me three years,
reason for that was

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:51.460
because they put me on
probation for three years

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:54.880
and I couldn't stay clean
long enough to pee clean.

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:58.150
So they kept on arresting me

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:02.210
for, you know, not going to
probation and stuff like that.

00:03:02.210 --> 00:03:06.660
So they, so they took me to
jail and I pulled a rehab card.

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:09.180
So, but I ran away from, to rehab.

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:11.400
I ran away when I got to rehab.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.580
So, I told the judge, I said,

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:18.040
I won't be able to stay
clean if I'm not, you know

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:20.670
gonna in a program, but
something like that.

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:23.020
And so you might as well
just send me down the road.

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:24.350
So that's what he did.

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:26.200
And I did two years, 11 months.

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:28.963
And I got out when I was 24.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:32.310
So I went in when I was right before

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:35.880
right before I turned 21.

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:40.410
So I spent my 21st birthday
in jail after that.

00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:44.170
- [Mark] And then you
came to LA after that?

00:03:44.170 --> 00:03:46.340
- Yeah, eight months later.

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:50.410
Cause I moved to Indianapolis
with him, my prison pen pal.

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:52.320
He was like a father figure.

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:56.560
And so, yeah, but I got on heroin

00:03:58.297 --> 00:04:01.050
when I was 19, which is a good
thing that I went to prison

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:06.050
because that's when the
heroin fentanyl epidemic came.

00:04:06.490 --> 00:04:10.250
And when I got out of prison,
all my friends were dead.

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:13.343
So it was kind of a blessing
that I went to prison.

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:17.720
- [Mark] And do you
have any friends today?

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:18.830
- No.

00:04:18.830 --> 00:04:20.400
- [Mark] You're just kind of on your own.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:21.233
And where do you live?

00:04:21.233 --> 00:04:22.324
You're in a tent.

00:04:22.324 --> 00:04:23.907
- I live in a tent.

00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:26.360
- And you, do you still work

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:27.370
for the pimp or are you on your own?

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:31.820
- No, I stopped messing with
that when it, since I was 18

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:36.473
but someone there has been,

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:41.410
you know, people trying to get at me,

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:44.823
but I know just to brush them off.

00:04:47.866 --> 00:04:48.880
- [Mark] And doing sex work,

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:51.500
have you, have you had some guys that have

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:54.414
given you a hard time
when you get picked up?

00:04:54.414 --> 00:04:56.580
Had some bad experiences?

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:57.973
- No, not really.

00:04:59.784 --> 00:05:01.467
I think that's why I've never been raped

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:06.467
because I go along with it,
you know, and I, you know

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:10.660
if I feel like it's, you know, bad or

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:13.510
if I'm getting to staying there too long

00:05:13.510 --> 00:05:15.760
and I feel like he's going
to do something to me,

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:18.990
then I find a gateway to
where I just run away.

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:22.410
You know, when he's like,
when I'm not near them.

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:23.480
But other than that--

00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:24.313
- [Mark] Escape.

00:05:24.313 --> 00:05:25.743
- I, I go along with it.

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:27.853
So.

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:31.610
- [Mark] And today your drug is what?

00:05:31.610 --> 00:05:33.130
Today you're using heroin?

00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:33.963
- Yes.

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:41.279
- [Mark] So you've been
arrested for what kind of stuff?

00:05:41.279 --> 00:05:46.279
- For GTA, taking my extra daddy's car

00:05:49.190 --> 00:05:52.513
but I returned it, but they,
the state picked it up.

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:59.143
And then I got, when I was 17,
got six trafficking charges.

00:06:01.049 --> 00:06:03.987
But the state said that
I was the youngest ever

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:07.300
in the state of Florida
to get these charges.

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:10.140
Which, I mean, I don't know
they were offering me 30 years,

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:14.400
but it took five years to, to beat it.

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:15.950
I beat it when I was in prison.

00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:19.553
- [Mark] So you were sex trafficking?

00:06:21.010 --> 00:06:23.747
- Yeah, I was sex trafficked when I was,

00:06:23.747 --> 00:06:27.750
when I was a young kid, you
know, when I was younger.

00:06:27.750 --> 00:06:31.183
And so I thought it was normal,
you know, recruiting girls

00:06:31.183 --> 00:06:32.283
- [Mark] Oh I see, so that's how you got

00:06:32.283 --> 00:06:33.260
the sex trafficking.
- And bring them on the team,

00:06:33.260 --> 00:06:34.093
you know.

00:06:34.093 --> 00:06:35.330
So I thought it was normal.

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:36.860
I didn't think I was doing anything wrong.

00:06:36.860 --> 00:06:40.950
And then when, when I had
gotten a little bit older

00:06:40.950 --> 00:06:45.590
like 16 then I hadn't, I was staying

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:47.320
in this foster home for a little bit

00:06:47.320 --> 00:06:50.710
and I had convinced my
bunkie to run away with me.

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:54.860
And so I was telling her my elaborate, my

00:06:54.860 --> 00:06:58.380
my lavish life, you know,
so, and she liked it.

00:06:58.380 --> 00:07:00.630
So that's how I got her, you know

00:07:00.630 --> 00:07:03.590
and I was showing her how
to do it, taking pictures

00:07:03.590 --> 00:07:07.070
and how to post and all
that, stuff like that.

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:10.800
And I ended up leaving,
leaving the pimp because he

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:13.390
he started to put his
hands on me, you know?

00:07:13.390 --> 00:07:15.900
And so she didn't want to go anywhere.

00:07:15.900 --> 00:07:17.490
So I was like, okay, fine.

00:07:17.490 --> 00:07:18.540
Stay with him.

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:21.120
Well, I called her the next
day when I was already away

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:21.953
from them.

00:07:21.953 --> 00:07:26.567
And she's like, "F you I'm
keeping all your stuff.

00:07:26.567 --> 00:07:28.408
"And he treats me good."

00:07:28.408 --> 00:07:30.730
And that was the last
thing I heard about her

00:07:30.730 --> 00:07:32.040
until like months down the road,

00:07:32.040 --> 00:07:34.320
I found out she gets caught up North

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:36.270
and because he's beating her.

00:07:36.270 --> 00:07:38.810
And then she tells the police that

00:07:38.810 --> 00:07:41.700
if it wasn't because of me, she
went and did all that stuff.

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:44.780
So that's what made them
charge me with sex trafficking

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:47.870
and procuring someone under
the age of 18 for prostitution,

00:07:47.870 --> 00:07:50.740
which I could have been
charged as a sex offender

00:07:50.740 --> 00:07:54.210
because I was, I ran away
until I was after 18.

00:07:54.210 --> 00:07:55.840
So they drug fouled me.

00:07:55.840 --> 00:07:57.642
So, but she was only like a couple months

00:07:57.642 --> 00:08:02.070
like two months younger
than me, but I dunno

00:08:02.070 --> 00:08:03.730
it was kind of retarded.

00:08:03.730 --> 00:08:06.220
But I ended up beating it too

00:08:06.220 --> 00:08:08.390
because they were offering me 30 years.

00:08:08.390 --> 00:08:10.520
But my lawyer was like, no

00:08:10.520 --> 00:08:13.130
