into what I was feeling

00:14:25.780 --> 00:14:28.840
but I just, I can't picture it.

00:14:28.840 --> 00:14:30.260
I used to be able to picture it

00:14:30.260 --> 00:14:34.773
but I just can't, I
can't picture a future.

00:14:39.638 --> 00:14:42.488
- [Mark] Do you ever feel
suicidal or anything like that?

00:14:48.170 --> 00:14:50.930
- Yeah, but I don't think on it, you know

00:14:54.240 --> 00:14:57.110
But lately I don't know.

00:14:57.110 --> 00:14:58.760
I don't really think about it.

00:14:58.760 --> 00:14:59.649
It's going to hurt.

00:14:59.649 --> 00:15:00.547
I don't really know.

00:15:00.547 --> 00:15:02.180
- [Mark] And you're a survivor.

00:15:02.180 --> 00:15:03.900
- Yeah, but I am scared of death.

00:15:03.900 --> 00:15:06.953
That's one thing I am scared of, to die.

00:15:08.900 --> 00:15:10.050
- [Mark] And living here on Skid Row

00:15:10.050 --> 00:15:12.140
have you had some bad
things happen to you here?

00:15:12.140 --> 00:15:12.980
- No.

00:15:12.980 --> 00:15:13.849
- [Mark] You haven't?

00:15:13.849 --> 00:15:16.110
- No.
- [Mark] Good for you.

00:15:16.110 --> 00:15:16.943
You're lucky.

00:15:16.943 --> 00:15:21.800
- I know a lot of people,
like a lot of big, big homies.

00:15:21.800 --> 00:15:26.170
They pulled me to the side
and they said the whole

00:15:26.170 --> 00:15:27.660
many years that I've been down here

00:15:27.660 --> 00:15:30.580
you're the first person
that I've seen able to walk

00:15:30.580 --> 00:15:32.170
on all the streets.

00:15:32.170 --> 00:15:35.170
And I don't know if it's
because I'm like a tourist,

00:15:35.170 --> 00:15:36.163
that's what I say.

00:15:37.070 --> 00:15:37.952
Cause I'm not from here.

00:15:37.952 --> 00:15:41.320
You know, I'm from Florida,
but I don't disrespect anybody.

00:15:41.320 --> 00:15:45.040
I just walk on the street
just like everyone else.

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:46.100
You know?

00:15:46.100 --> 00:15:48.560
Cause I, I thought about California.

00:15:48.560 --> 00:15:49.393
This is why I thought

00:15:49.393 --> 00:15:51.980
about California in that I wasn't going to

00:15:51.980 --> 00:15:54.830
be able to wear this Navy
blue shirt down the street.

00:15:54.830 --> 00:15:58.827
You know that's how they projected
what California was like.

00:15:58.827 --> 00:15:59.920
And so I got here?

00:15:59.920 --> 00:16:01.310
And then I'm like, okay

00:16:02.530 --> 00:16:04.793
It's pretty, it's not that bad.

00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:07.793
- [Mark] Do you miss Florida?

00:16:09.840 --> 00:16:12.713
- I miss the beaches, yeah.

00:16:14.560 --> 00:16:15.710
- [Mark] What do you, what
do you wish was different

00:16:15.710 --> 00:16:16.810
about your life today?

00:16:18.400 --> 00:16:20.583
What do you think would
help you the most right now?

00:16:25.850 --> 00:16:29.133
- What do I think would
be different you said?

00:16:29.133 --> 00:16:31.180
- [Mark] What do you like,

00:16:31.180 --> 00:16:32.670
what would help you the most right now?

00:16:32.670 --> 00:16:34.820
You're, you're in a jam
kinda, living homeless

00:16:34.820 --> 00:16:38.350
and addicted to drugs and
doing sex work for money.

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:41.580
And it's just, it's a
tough corner you're in.

00:16:41.580 --> 00:16:43.280
I'm just wondering what
would it like if there

00:16:43.280 --> 00:16:46.130
was one thing that could
change things for you

00:16:46.130 --> 00:16:49.133
what, what do you think that would be?

00:16:56.513 --> 00:16:58.720
- To not have told my pastor

00:16:58.720 --> 00:17:00.653
about what was going on at home.

00:17:01.920 --> 00:17:04.380
- [Mark] Yeah, dealing with that.

00:17:04.380 --> 00:17:07.010
Is that what the drug drug use
has kind of like numbing you

00:17:07.010 --> 00:17:07.843
from that pain?

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:11.710
- I forgave my stepdad

00:17:11.710 --> 00:17:14.883
and I just haven't forgotten
my mom because she,

00:17:16.860 --> 00:17:18.983
like, she doesn't believe me, you know?

00:17:22.286 --> 00:17:25.957
And I wish I could take
like a lie detector test

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:32.793
and give it to her and walk
away and never see her again.

00:17:34.760 --> 00:17:36.363
- [Mark] So your mom doesn't believe you?

00:17:40.494 --> 00:17:42.960
- [Madison] No, that's
why I can't move on.

00:17:42.960 --> 00:17:46.672
I know it sounds stupid,
but it's just reality,

00:17:46.672 --> 00:17:48.837
that's how I feel.

00:17:48.837 --> 00:17:51.150
I feel like I'm stuck in that.

00:17:51.150 --> 00:17:52.270
I'm just stuck I haven't grew up.

00:17:52.270 --> 00:17:55.453
I haven't, I'm just stuck.

00:18:00.030 --> 00:18:00.961
- [Mark] All right, Madison,

00:18:00.961 --> 00:18:02.723
well thank you so much
for sharing your story.

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:06.500
I hope you, I hope your
life gets a little better.

00:18:06.500 --> 00:18:08.580
I hope you figure some, some way off

00:18:08.580 --> 00:18:10.380
off of Skid Row and get out of here.

00:18:12.610 --> 00:18:13.610
Thank you very much.

